<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Sports</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:46Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-sports" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-8171?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-sports" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Bayern Munich bosses under fire over Jamal Musiala comments</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:be2c1edc40c2ce9dab863c881c723b6e63a8583bc699d707437838ea0e859440</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-22T11:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187--78383bcfae5b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-bosses-under-fire-over-jamal-musiala-comments/a-80013187?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Officials have publicly questioned whether Musiala will ever fully recover from a debilitating neurological condition and queried the validity of his contract, prompting criticism from fans, media and the FIFPRO union.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich head coach Vincent Kompany's health scare highlights the need for better support for elite coaches</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1707c345dab6b759eb06bdace4c8ffb0b4571b93b57dbf312c03b1d2f1d09408</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-29T07:43:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-e/a-79764661--fcbaed2aac2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-head-coach-vincent-kompany-s-health-scare-highlights-the-need-for-better-support-for-elite-coaches/a-79764661?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Vincent Kompany’s health concern is a reminder that elite football's pressures affect coaches too. Better support, clearer structures and mental health safeguards are increasingly vital.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala collapses on pitch again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4977d186d5c3a0e2b635fe00fc83d9540953eafe534160cfdfbd1b89ce24c3dc</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:23:46Z</updated><published>2026-08-19T10:22:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021--e8b1c3225cf9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bayern-munich-s-jamal-musiala-collapses-on-pitch-again/a-78426021?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">One of Germany's top footballers has collapsed on the pitch for a second time in four days ahead of the new season. Bayern Munich's Jamal Musiala has said he has a "neurological dysfunction" that causes blackouts.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>US and UK to host Women's World Cups in 2031 and 2035</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4f046b9723c1e408d7e3f7cf43a3baba70c77945984d673f58170caaee6dd327</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T16:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786--81630f151694.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-and-uk-to-host-women-s-world-cups-in-2031-and-2035/a-80023786?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">FIFA has confirmed the United States, Mexico, Costa Rica and Jamaica will host the 2031 Women's World Cup — the first to feature 48 teams. The UK will stage the 2035 edition, its first World Cup since 1966.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gukesh to defend chess crown against rising star Sindarov</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e37a273253336cf4acbf92f2d3e36c58ffae6f0137e5742df57910fdc88ed7b2</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-23T15:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806--07e5204aa07f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gukesh-to-defend-chess-crown-against-rising-star-sindarov/a-80021806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the World Chess championship gets underway, it's no coincidence that the titleholder, Gukesh Dommaraju, and his challenger, Jakhovir Sindarov, are both from Asia.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>FIFA presidential election 2027: Infantino facing Diallo and Tashima — could an alliance change everything?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a3cc163005f24f3801a3b23eba3c01a7162d711734f421f701ff4464e005b809</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-20T12:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everyth/a-80002882--01040a665cff.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifa-presidential-election-2027-infantino-facing-diallo-and-tashima-could-an-alliance-change-everything/a-80002882?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Two challengers to Gianni Infantino have registered for next year's FIFA presidential election. What do Philippe Diallo and Kozo Tashima stand for – and do they stand a chance against the incumbent?</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Alexander Zverev faces fresh lawsuit from ex-girlfriend</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6feb499a345dcffafd439165f76782adf2327a2c66f1769e2d5a47993664c7dd</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-19T15:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005--d63dbeaa4aae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/alexander-zverev-faces-fresh-lawsuit-from-ex-girlfriend/a-79990005?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">World No. 1 tennis player Alexander Zverev is facing a new lawsuit related to a domestic abuse trial. The lawyer for his ex-girlfriend, Brenda Patea, told DW what the allegations are against the German player.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund bows to fan pressure and end Rheinmetall deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ff88acbc16891a8a43b2262bf4762475a65575d50fd4917543d76845f1c03dbb</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-18T15:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121--2c9b64a964f9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-bows-to-fan-pressure-and-end-rheinmetall-deal/a-79980121?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Borussia Dortmund has reluctantly ended its association with a major sponsor after long-term fan protests. They are not the first Bundesliga club to u-turn, as commercial interests clash with politics and fan culture.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp and Wirtz offer glimpse of bright German future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e86490707719edbd882e4a418a739c8aeabc7d3f0b8a3d7c4d7a96b97c192412</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-17T11:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184--a5059b3200c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-and-wirtz-offer-glimpse-of-bright-german-future/a-79968184?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's fall from grace in recent years has seen the team drift away from the fans. But Monday's drubbing of the Netherlands and the impact of Jürgen Klopp, Florian Wirtz and emerging youngsters offers hope.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Klopp wants Infantino out as FIFA candidate deadline looms</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:364dfff25dea55708f3fa0830298743c96547237aabba3c89aa39c2f66c2416b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-16T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229--458d3356c9f8.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/klopp-wants-infantino-out-as-fifa-candidate-deadline-looms/a-79958229?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany coach Jürgen Klopp has joined the chorus of football figures critical of FIFA President Gianni Infantino. But with time running out, there are few who seem willing to run against him.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Russia is back in world sport, but who is drug testing its athletes?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:919eae9649440771979717b4469ca28c76958582b4812310c7ab2b65c5b5f98b</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-05T14:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467--6f0e1f90efa4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russia-is-back-in-world-sport-but-who-is-drug-testing-its-athletes/a-79862467?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">DW has found that three-quarters of Russia's weightlifting team had no independent out-of-competition testing before this year's world championships, despite the country's doping history.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Gold for the West Bank: Meet Palestinian karate champ Mariam Bsharat</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e12041533f118678ca4d05050817fcf719e681990a0232ced084e5cc7c6a7199</id><updated>2026-11-23T20:22:12Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T15:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806--7b674acad5ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gold-for-the-west-bank-meet-palestinian-karate-champ-mariam-bsharat/a-79851806?maca=en-rss-en-sports-1027-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The occupied West Bank is not an obvious breeding ground for sporting success. But Mariam Bsharat, 17, has beaten the odds to become a karate world champion and is making a new life in Germany.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
